From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Cemin <dcemin@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:09:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: soundwire: mediatek: reset the PDI FIFO in
 prepare

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2166301

A stop/start cycle on an open PCM (desktop sound test, PipeWire) never
passes through hw_params/hw_free, and the prepare callback only
reprograms the DAI when it resumes from system sleep, so the PDI FIFO
is never reset between cycles. ASoC runs the STOP triggers in reverse
order: this CPU DAI disables the PDI engen first, and the dai_link
trigger then stops the manager port with sdw_disable_stream(), so
whatever was in flight between the two stays in the FIFO. On the
2-channel interleaved jack PDI (DL1 -> PDI5 -> RT712 DP5) an odd
residue shifts the word phase, and from the next START on the left
sample lands in the right slot. Observed as a left/right swap after a
few rapid clicks on "Test Front Left", and reproduced at the ALSA level
with the PCM held open: the channel alternates on every
drain/prepare/start cycle.

Reset every PDI of the DAI in prepare, which runs after the previous
STOP has completed on both the PDI and the manager port side, so every
START begins with an empty FIFO. Eight consecutive held-open cycles
stay on the left channel with this change.

Signed-off-by: David Cemin <dcemin@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit 797d3dd76569d727ae3bf405f6fba2facce87291 resolute:linux-nvidia-bos)
Signed-off-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00686
Ledger-Origin: nvidia@45757677f3092cb55bc2d264ac8c9e5f43ffbf7e
---
 drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c | 43 +++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c b/drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c
index 71671ebb0963..a14df4834c24 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c
@@ -550,25 +550,36 @@ static int mtk_sdw_dai_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	struct mtk_sdw_port_params mtk_port_param = { 0 };
 	int i, dir;
 
-	if (!mdai->suspended)
-		return 0;
-
-	mdai->suspended = false;
-
-	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE)
-		dir = SDW_DATA_DIR_RX;
-	else
-		dir = SDW_DATA_DIR_TX;
-
-	mtk_port_param.port_num = mdai->port_num;
-	mtk_port_param.bpt_payload_type = 0;
-	mtk_port_param.bpt_en = true;
-	mtk_sdw_configure_port_params(&mdai->link->core, &mtk_port_param, dir);
+	if (mdai->suspended) {
+		mdai->suspended = false;
+
+		if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE)
+			dir = SDW_DATA_DIR_RX;
+		else
+			dir = SDW_DATA_DIR_TX;
+
+		mtk_port_param.port_num = mdai->port_num;
+		mtk_port_param.bpt_payload_type = 0;
+		mtk_port_param.bpt_en = true;
+		mtk_sdw_configure_port_params(&mdai->link->core, &mtk_port_param,
+					      dir);
+	}
 
-	for (i = 0; i < mdai->pdi_count; i++) {
+	/*
+	 * ASoC runs the STOP triggers in reverse order: this DAI disables the
+	 * PDI engen first and the dai_link trigger then stops the manager port
+	 * (sdw_disable_stream), so whatever was in flight between the two
+	 * stays in the PDI FIFO. On a 2-channel interleaved PDI an odd number
+	 * of stale words shifts the word phase and the next START swaps left
+	 * and right for the rest of the PCM's life. A stop/start cycle on an
+	 * open PCM never passes hw_params/hw_free, so reset every PDI here,
+	 * where the previous STOP has completed on both sides and nothing
+	 * feeds or drains the FIFO. Re-writing the same channel mask and port
+	 * number is harmless.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < mdai->pdi_count; i++)
 		mtk_sdw_configure_pdi_params(&mdai->link->core,
 					     &mdai->pdi_params[i]);
-	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
